                <pb facs="0794" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg710"/>

                <head>No. 332.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 13, 1886</date>.
                        (Received August 13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Jackson informs Mr. Bayard that the government of Coahuila asserts that
                    Arresures was by law a Mexican and a fugitive from justice; and that after he
                    had been extradited, and while he was being conducted to court, he took flight,
                    and, in the pursuit that followed, was killed.</p>
            </div>
